> I have only one remark: I feel that "Elbereth" shouldn't be spammable
> with a command like ^e. I may be more lazy than average players, but I
> remember having quite a few YASD which could have been avoided if I
> felt like engraving (more) E-word.

In my opinion, the most basic fact (which Un and Spork acknowledge, but 
vanilla never did) is that there is a problem with Elbereth. It has the 
charm of being both a desaster interface-wise as well as a dubious design 
in terms of balance (since players can rely on it versus monsters, some of 
them relevant very late). As I see it, there are several interesting 
options:

a) simply remove Elbereth
This takes care of both issues, but loses a bit of flavour. (And makes the 
game harder, which might be a problem for those who think that 100% 
winnability is the target.)

b) nerf Elbereth so as to be useless past some (early) point
If I understand correctly, this is the path that Spork has chosen. This 
takes care of the balance issue and assume that the interface annoyance is 
bearable (because the feature loses usefulness quick enough).

c) make Elbereth as easy command
This is the UnNethack approach, it seems. However, it completely neglects 
the balance problems. (Un may have taken care of them in previous 
releases; I do not know).

I share solidsnail's sentiment that solution c) is a bit lackluster. 
Speaking as a designer, I don't like using interface niceties as a bandaid 
to tape over balance issues.

But enough of that, it is very good to see the forks being alive!
